Package: elitebook-thermal-profile
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3,
         systemd,
         udev
Recommends: ryzenadj (>= 0.17.0)
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-elitebook-thermal-profile
Description: thermal and power profiles for HP AMD Cezanne laptops
 User-space thermal and power profile integration for selected HP EliteBook and
 ProBook AMD Cezanne laptops. It combines AMD P-State EPP, CPU frequency policy,
 systemd units, udev rules, and RyzenAdj-driven SMU limits into a profile
 dispatcher with idle, AC/battery, update guard, and Steam game automation.
 .
 Full SMU control requires a RyzenAdj binary, which Debian and Ubuntu do not
 package. Without it the profiles degrade to kernel EPP, boost, and frequency
 controls where the driver exposes them.
 .
 Installing this package deliberately does not start hardware tuning. Enable the
 units explicitly after checking that your machine is on the supported hardware
 list.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-elitebook-thermal-profile
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         elitebook-thermal-profile (= ${binary:Version}),
         gnome-shell (>= 45),
         pkexec
Description: GNOME Shell indicator for EliteBook thermal profiles
 GNOME Shell panel indicator for switching the EliteBook thermal profile between
 Auto, Game, and Quiet without exposing lower-level technical profiles in the
 daily user interface.
 .
 The extension must be enabled once after installation with
 gnome-extensions enable elitebook-thermal-profile@matteopasseri.github.io
